# Context for the api image (`docker build -f api/Dockerfile .` from the repo
# root). Everything is out except the api and the marking engine it installs;
# web/ and the voice workers build from their own folders.
*
!api
!assessment/packages/osce_assessment

# SEC-009: keep secrets, local state and cruft out of the build context so they
# never reach the image or a build cache.
**/.git
**/.venv
**/__pycache__
**/*.pyc
**/.pytest_cache
**/.mypy_cache
**/.ruff_cache
**/.env
**/.env.*
!api/.env.example
**/*.pem
**/*.key
**/serviceAccountKey.json
**/*serviceAccount*.json
**/.DS_Store
**/*.log

# Engine build leftovers from a local `poetry install`.
assessment/packages/osce_assessment/build
assessment/packages/osce_assessment/*.egg-info

# Api files not needed at runtime. The engine keeps its README: its
# pyproject names it, and the install fails without it.
api/docker-compose.yml
api/docker-compose.*.yml
api/*.md
api/docs
api/tests
api/htmlcov
api/.coverage
api/coverage.xml
api/logs
